---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How This Site Works | Aoun Md."
  description="A look at the architecture and engineering decisions behind Aoun Md.'s personal portfolio."
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE WEBSITE / ENGINEERING NOTES</p>

      <h1 class="page-title">
        Small infrastructure.
        <span class="serif-accent">Intentional decisions.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="page-description">
        This website is also an opportunity to apply the same engineering
        principles I use in larger projects: clear architecture, automation,
        security, performance, and maintainability.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-border">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="case-article">
        <h2>Why a static architecture?</h2>

        <p>
          A professional portfolio primarily delivers content. It does not need
          a persistent application server, database, or Kubernetes cluster.
        </p>

        <p>
          I chose Astro to generate pages at build time and keep the amount of
          JavaScript sent to visitors small.
        </p>

        <h2>Design and content</h2>

        <p>
          The website uses a custom visual system, responsive layouts,
          self-hosted typography, optimized images, and project case studies
          maintained as Markdown.
        </p>

        <p>
          The case studies document the actual engineering work behind my
          projects rather than relying only on a list of technologies.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>

        <p>
          The site is designed for GitHub Pages, with a static build and no
          continuously running cloud infrastructure.
        </p>

        <p>
          This keeps hosting costs low and avoids operational complexity that
          would not improve the experience.
        </p>

        <h2>Automation and quality</h2>

        <p>
          GitHub Actions validates the Astro project, builds the static
          website, and runs Playwright browser and automated accessibility
          checks. A separate release job builds the GitHub Pages artifact,
          which is published after the required workflow dependencies pass.
        </p>

        <p>
          The repository uses pull requests to review changes before
          publication. The deployment workflow and supporting tests
          are maintained alongside the website source.
        </p>

        <h2>Performance and accessibility</h2>

        <p>
          The implementation prioritizes readable content, keyboard navigation,
          responsive layouts, optimized photography, and reduced-motion
          preferences.
        </p>

        <p>
          Visual effects should support the content. They should not delay
          access to project information or make the website harder to use.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics and privacy</h2>

        <p>
          This website uses Cloudflare Web Analytics when the analytics
          integration is enabled. It provides aggregate information about
          visits and page performance.
        </p>

        <p>
          The website does not use advertising trackers, visitor accounts,
          or a custom contact-form database. Analytics requests are
          processed by Cloudflare, and privacy tools or browser settings
          may block them.
        </p>

        <p>
          The website's main content and navigation remain available
          without the analytics script.
        </p>

        <h2>Source code</h2>

        <p>
          The website source is maintained in a public GitHub repository:
          <a href="https://github.com/Aoun62336/Aoun62336.github.io">
            Aoun62336.github.io
          </a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
